{
  "item": "Object19",
  "mu_name": "Object19",
  "mu_name_from": "Noria's object slot 18, which is the model index: every world but Lorencia runs its objects in one straight sequence, so type N is Object{N+1}.bmd and there is no friendlier name in the client than the number.",
  "world": "noria",
  "object_type": 18,
  "placements": 2,
  "profile": "world",
  "sheets": {
    "flower7": "nr_flower7.png",
    "wood01": "nr_wood01.png",
    "filling_up05": "nr_filling_up05.png",
    "metal01": "nr_metal01.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Data/Object4/*.OZJ and .OZT, from MuMain, decoded under an nr_ prefix. The prefix is load-bearing for the reason the ground's is: assets/textures is one flat pool for every world, and yellow_jewel.png was already taken by an item.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "flower7": "bark",
    "wood01": "plank",
    "filling_up05": "foliage",
    "metal01": "wrought_iron"
  },
  "material_note": "flower7: grey-brown bark. Named flower and is a tree.\nwood01: sawn light boards.\nfilling_up05: a climbing vine, cut out at 80%.\nmetal01: mottled grey metal.",
  "cutout": [
    "filling_up05"
  ],
  "cutout_from": "Each carries a real alpha channel, as decode_texture reports it. Declared rather than detected - three separate attempts to read a cut-out off the art have been wrong, and the client decides it in code.",
  "additive": [
    "filling_up05"
  ],
  "additive_from": "ZzzObject.cpp, CreateObject, case WD_3NORIA: `o->BlendMesh = 2` for type 18, and the render path draws that submesh with RENDER_BRIGHT. Mesh order is the .bmd's, which is the order the .obj groups are in.",
  "glow": {
    "filling_up05": {
      "scrolls_per_second": -1.0
    }
  },
  "glow_from": "ZzzObject.cpp, MoveObject, case WD_3NORIA: `o->BlendMeshTexCoordV = (int)WorldTime % 1000 * 0.001f` for type 18, whose BlendMesh CreateObject sets to 2 - filling_up05. One repetition a second, upward, so -1 in scrolls_per_second's sense. See Object42.",
